* GND/VCC bounce model - SN74ALVC244 SOIC (DW), IBIS component ALVC244_DW - board ref Q3
* Driver: linear model, pull-up/pull-down resistors controlled by the input (Ron = Rdrv, 500 ps ramp).
* Package: IBIS [Pin] R_pin, L_pin in series with C_pin split as C/2 at each end (pi). Shared die rails VCC_DIE / GND_DIE.
* Lines: Rs (39R) + lossless T-line (50R, 600 ps) + receiver C (next SN74ALVC244 input). Monitor: no Rs, scope 50R at the end.
* Run: one simulation steps Nact = 1, 3, 7 active lines. Set MON=0 for GND bounce (monitor low), MON=1 for VCC bounce (monitor high).
* Plot V(gnd_die) or V(vcc_die) (internal rails) and V(mon_scope) (what the scope sees), with V(l1_rx) as timing reference.
* Board supply (LDO 3.3 V, plane) + 100 nF decoupling
* C73/C79 100nF 0805
* VCC pin 20 (IBIS): C/2 - R - L - C/2
* GND pin 10 (IBIS)
* on-die
* VCC-GND C
* Clock 20 MHz, 0..1 V control, 500 ps edges (buffer input)        8th-line control (MON)
* Simulation settings (MON: 0 = 8th line low -> GND bounce, 1 = high -> VCC bounce)
.include bounce_models.lib
.param MON=1
.step param Nact list 1 3 7
.param Rdrv=11 Rs=39 Z0line=50 TDline=600p Crx=5p Ccomp=6.04p Cdie=20p Tr=500p
.tran 0 60n 0 5p
.options plotwinsize=0
.options method=gear
.meas TRAN GND_max MAX V(GND_DIE) FROM 4n TO 60n
.meas TRAN GND_min MIN V(GND_DIE) FROM 4n TO 60n
.meas TRAN VCC_max MAX V(VCC_DIE) FROM 4n TO 60n
.meas TRAN VCC_min MIN V(VCC_DIE) FROM 4n TO 60n
.meas TRAN MON_dc FIND V(MON_SCOPE) AT 4n
.meas TRAN MON_max MAX V(MON_SCOPE) FROM 4n TO 60n
.meas TRAN MON_min MIN V(MON_SCOPE) FROM 4n TO 60n
* Results of .meas: View > SPICE Error Log (one set per step of Nact).
* Parameters: Rdrv driver output R (assignment: 11R), Rs series R (39R),
* Z0line/TDline T-line (50R / 600 ps), Crx receiver input C (4.21p C_comp + pin C),
* Ccomp driver die capacitance (IBIS ALVC244_OUT_33 C_comp typ), split half to each rail
* (the IBIS file lists C_pullup ~ C_pulldown). Cdie = on-die VCC-GND capacitance (estimate, not in IBIS).
* Board PDN values (L_brd, R_brd, L_esl, R_esr) are estimates - tune them to match measurements.
* scope 50R (P40, ch2 1x)
* MON: 2Y4 (pin 3) - 8th line (monitor): held at MON, input 2A4 set by J3/J6
* L1: 2Y3 (pin 5) - toggles for N=1,3,7 (2A3 <- clock bank 2, J8)
* L2: 1Y1 (pin 18) - toggles for N=3,7; Hi-Z for N=1 (1OE off)
* L3: 1Y2 (pin 16) - toggles for N=3,7; Hi-Z for N=1 (1OE off)
* L4: 1Y3 (pin 14) - toggles for N=7; quiet low N=3; Hi-Z N=1
* L5: 1Y4 (pin 12) - toggles for N=7; quiet low N=3; Hi-Z N=1
* L6: 2Y1 (pin 9) - toggles for N=7; quiet low for N=1,3
* L7: 2Y2 (pin 7) - toggles for N=7; quiet low for N=1,3
.backanno
.end
